; Regression: a `set` whose target is a NON-MUTABLE reference and whose source
; stores through nothing is a hard error (2026-08-27).
;
; The emitter's Variable arm returns without storing when the target is not
; `is_mutable`, so such a statement is a SILENT no-op. That is how three
; `store %Entity` vanished out of opensp's parse_external_entity during the
; deref sweep -- the SGML corpus went 380/380 to 287/380, every failure an
; entity or a subdoc, with nothing said at the line that caused it.
;
; A `var` local may be rebound; a parameter and a `let` may not, so there the
; only reading left is the store, and a value that is neither the pointee nor
; a reference of the same type has no reading at all.
;
; xfail: cannot assign through this reference

define Box (v: int)

procedure wrong(r: ref[Box], n: int)
{
    set r: n
}

var b Box(1)
wrong(&b, 5)
Console.println "unreachable"
